          "rationale": "Section 14.2(B) contains a genuine Vendor-side defend-and-indemnify obligation running to Customer, expressly covering third-party IP infringement claims against the Services and M&I software, M&I's violation of protective laws, and financial/property loss from M&I's acts or omissions — and it carries no customer-modification/combination exclusions, so it sits at or above the preferred position on scope. Section 14.3 supplies standard procedure (notice, indemnitor control with reasonable counsel, cooperation, settlement consent), and costs of enforcement are on M&I. Minor points noted but not flagged: there is no express limb for unauthorised access to Customer Data (largely picked up by the broad \"acts or omissions\" limb), and the reciprocal Customer indemnity in 14.2(A) is broader than our preferred content/breach-of-law-only formulation, though it mirrors M&I's own obligation. Separately, Section 13.4 caps M&I's total liability at three months' fees \"[n]otwithstanding any provision in this Agreement\", which would also cut down the indemnity; that cap is the subject of the limitation-of-liability rule and is not double-flagged here.",
